[{:db/id "q-79330/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "e93a9665-2338-5665-a5fb-0695e3b625bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79330/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "85570b73-32ed-53d3-9cac-646d81e759b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79330/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f246ebc7-45e4-5632-8c1c-03c9ed1a380a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79330/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "278ca932-6bd2-5409-a12c-59e55f3a91f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79330/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1fb93bf5-9543-57f8-bc26-332e5dccb902" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79330/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75d3c876-9a73-5d7f-be91-1b4288459661" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79330/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-79330/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-79330/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-79330/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-79330/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-79330/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79330" :question/id #uuid "df42d33c-ab0b-52f4-82a5-1108ad30f682" :question/math-academy-id "q-79330" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y={e}^{-4x}$\n- $y={e}^{4x}$\n- $y=4{e}^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{-4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{-4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ -4{e}^{-4x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{-4x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 8{e}^{-4x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{4x} & =4{e}^{4x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y={e}^{4x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=4{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4(4{e}^{x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}16{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 12{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=4{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79330/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79330"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141092/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "af616c88-26d1-5b72-b19c-57726efe8a77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141092/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "9f5c5dbf-cfb2-5f71-809b-221068a282fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141092/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7786dcac-bd13-5ba2-a4d8-028bb77023e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141092/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "6230f0e6-d0a4-5251-bc20-ccbe2b374168" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141092/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "178e8522-f6d6-5615-a7db-e649a18d2cad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141092/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3231972-1caa-5cea-86d8-e37996473f0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141092/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-141092/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-141092/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-141092/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-141092/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-141092/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141092" :question/id #uuid "6bc95deb-40f2-508a-aa44-de7fe1d1479e" :question/math-academy-id "q-141092" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-141092/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80ed79a9-8e39-5c84-9c87-dec266060afc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141092"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141107/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "c7868473-ef33-540e-afff-2111b32510ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141107/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "00936aaf-aa47-5f4c-8b88-98068c612fa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141107/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "2f4284e2-6405-5af1-8e18-6ed7e5f0ceb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141107/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "e80c9a44-9797-521d-8a6b-d9408f81ba46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141107/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "731f18bd-d7d6-51a1-b655-6def4699992a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141107/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33a69b8c-cfd3-597e-be8d-e19a8a9f044c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141107/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-141107/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-141107/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-141107/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-141107/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-141107/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141107" :question/id #uuid "d7f17189-7b82-5218-afd5-ddec775b868c" :question/math-academy-id "q-141107" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,y(-1)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{x}^{4}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{x}^{4}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-1)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{x}^{4} \\\\ -1 & =A(-1)^{4} \\\\ -1 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=(-1){x}^{4}=-{x}^{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141107/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141107"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141116/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "a005a8c3-1eb7-5608-bf28-850aabbb8a35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141116/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "191114dc-6acc-568b-9cc5-d71bfeca996b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141116/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6632709a-3d7c-5ba7-a42f-db9b5d4aec6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141116/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "3c94db7b-8874-5d6d-b048-2fd3ff11f860" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141116/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "7cf05be1-4507-5c1a-8a3c-31ab08cc9d20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141116/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "65cab405-7421-5b6f-a5c2-a8b4adeaf231" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141116/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-141116/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-141116/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-141116/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-141116/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-141116/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141116" :question/id #uuid "ea6ff592-81a4-59f3-84d6-c97bdc2e3a4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-141116" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{1}{A+x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=\\frac{1}{A+x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{A+x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{A+0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{A} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2+x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141116/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141116"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352660/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "283c827a-e42f-5a0a-a767-1f40d3564e0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352660/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7462996-4474-52b4-8b55-d9744d03b6e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352660/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-352660/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352660" :question/id #uuid "0ad1b80f-f6b4-5a82-9600-dba1f5e03f4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-352660" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{4y}{x},\\,y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{A}{{2}^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{A}{16} \\\\ A & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352660/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352660"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
